---
description: Git remotes and push/fetch MUST use SSH only — never HTTPS
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git: SSH only

- **NEVER** use `https://github.com/...` for `git remote`, `git push`, `git fetch`, `git pull`, or one-off push URLs.
- If SSH fails (`Permission denied (publickey)`), **stop** and tell the user. Do not invent an HTTPS fallback.

| Remote | URL |
|--------|-----|
| `origin` | `git@github.com:DevNathan/ftl-dev.vim.git` |
